  "result": "The customer was right, and it's fixed. The discount check in `shop/pricing.py:10` used `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD`, so with the threshold at 10, an order of exactly 10 units was left out. The policy says 10 or more.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the check to `line.qty >= BULK_THRESHOLD`.\n\n**Tests:** One existing test, `test_bulk_discount`, already covered this case and was failing before the change. For 10 units at $1.00 it expects $9.50 plus 8.25% tax, which is $10.28. The code was returning $10.83, the full price plus tax. I also added `test_no_bulk_discount_below_threshold`, which checks that 9 units still get no discount. All 7 tests now pass.\n\nNo other code uses the threshold. Because the cart combines repeat additions of the same item into one line, 5 + 5 of an item also gets the discount, which matches the policy.",
